{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792593936,"nonce":"7DTqLRPTzvPRc7vRJBetjpI93nc=","title":"Virtualize completion rows and release hidden completion candidates","message":"The LSP memory probe reproduces large allocation spikes in completion UI with both Haxe display fallback and Rayzor. Ashui CodeCompletions builds up to 200 rows while only 10 are visible, and hide() retains its items and rows signals until another list replaces them or the editor is disposed. In matched 58-tab probes, five completion opens allocated 2880.7 MiB with fallback and 339.9 MiB with Rayzor; physical footprint at the phase checkpoint was 783.6 / 671.8 MiB and settled to 467.6 / 480.5 MiB after collection. These are whole-phase measurements, not an attribution of every byte to rows. Next steps: virtualize visible completion rows with overscan, clear candidate/row metadata on hide (including zero-match/invalid-anchor early returns), and verify that delayed old popup closure cannot clear a replacement list. Evidence: bin/lsp-memory-58-before/results.json, tests/LspMemoryProbe.hx, pinned Ashui components/code/CodeCompletions.hx.","files":null}]}